    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Leader of the Starry Skies: A Tribute to Tim Smith, Songbook 1 is a charity compilation released in December 2010 on the Believers Roast label. The album emerged as a response to Tim Smith's severe stroke in 2008, which left the Cardiacs founder and principal songwriter unable to perform or work. Rather than a conventional tribute, the project united a diverse roster of artists—including Oceansize, The Magic Numbers, Steven Wilson, Ultrasound, and Knifeworld—to celebrate Smith's compositional legacy while raising funds for his recovery and care. All profits from the album's sales were directed entirely to Smith.\n\nThe compilation spans electronic and rock territories, reflecting the eclectic nature of Smith's influence across progressive and alternative music communities. The 17-track collection features reinterpretations of Smith's compositions, with contributions ranging from established acts to lesser-known projects, demonstrating the breadth of his artistic reach and the affection he commanded among musicians. Notable appearances include collaborations such as Max Tundra's \"Will Bleed Amen\" featuring Sarah Measures and Robert White's \"Lilywhite's Party\" with Andy Partridge, showcasing the collaborative spirit of the endeavor.\n\nThe album achieved modest commercial circulation through both physical and digital formats, with vinyl and CD editions released through Genepool distribution. While not a mainstream commercial success, the project succeeded in its primary mission as a benefit album, functioning as both a musical document of Smith's songwriting significance and a tangible expression of support from the progressive music community during a critical period in his life.",
      "generated_at": "2025-11-27T16:27:17.779292",
